    "\n",
    "In Part 2, the focus shifts to data retrieval and insights. Several SQL queries are developed to extract complex information from the database. These queries answer analytical questions such as identifying physicians responsible for drug-related alerts, examining adverse drug interactions, evaluating pricing patterns, and calculating pharmacy markups. The queries also explore time-based prescription behavior and patient non-compliance.\n",
    "\n",
    "Additionally, an optional bonus task is included, which involves implementing a SQL trigger. This trigger automatically inserts a record into the alerts table whenever a newly prescribed drug adversely interacts with a previously prescribed drug for the same patient.\n",
    "\n",
    "Overall, this project demonstrates real-world database skills such as schema implementation, data integration, complex querying, and trigger-based automation—all essential for working with healthcare and other domain-specific datasets."
