    "#  Database Schema\n",
    "\n",
    "This schema defines the structure for a healthcare system involving patients, physicians, drugs, pharmacies, and pharmaceutical companies. Below is a breakdown of each table, its attributes, and relationships with other tables.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1. patients\n",
    "\n",
    "**Definition:** Contains personal and health-related information about patients.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Attributes:**\n",
    "- `ssn` – Primary Key, unique identifier for the patient\n",
    "- `name` – Patient's full name\n",
    "- `address` – Residential address\n",
    "- `birth_date` – Date of birth\n",
    "- `physician_id` – Foreign Key → `physicians(ssn)`, referring to the patient's primary physician\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2. physicians\n",
    "\n",
    "**Definition:** Contains details of physicians working in the system.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Attributes:**\n",
    "- `ssn` – Primary Key, unique identifier for the physician\n",
    "- `name` – Full name of the physician\n",
    "- `primary_specialty` – Medical specialty (e.g., Cardiology, Dermatology)\n",
    "- `experience_years` – Total years of experience\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3. pharmacies\n",
    "\n",
    "**Definition:** Stores information about pharmacies that fill prescriptions.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Attributes:**\n",
    "- `id` – Primary Key, unique identifier for the pharmacy\n",
    "- `name` – Pharmacy name\n",
    "- `address` – Physical address\n",
    "- `phone` – Contact number\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "### 4. drugs\n",
    "\n",
    "**Definition:** Contains a list of all available prescription drugs.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Attributes:**\n",
    "- `id` – Primary Key, unique identifier for the drug\n",
    "- `name` – Drug name\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "### 5. prescriptions\n",
    "\n",
    "**Definition:** Records each prescription issued to a patient.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Attributes:**\n",
    "- `id` – Primary Key\n",
    "- `patient_id` – Foreign Key → `patients(ssn)`\n",
    "- `physician_id` – Foreign Key → `physicians(ssn)`\n",
    "- `drug_name` – Foreign Key → `drugs(name)`\n",
    "- `date` – Date of prescription\n",
    "- `quantity` – Amount prescribed\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "### 6. adverse_interactions\n",
    "\n",
    "**Definition:** Defines drug pairs that may cause adverse interactions when used together.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Attributes:**\n",
    "- `drug_name` – Foreign Key → `drugs(name)`\n",
    "- `drug_name` – Foreign Key → `drugs(name)`  \n",
    "*(Each row represents a drug interaction between two drugs.)*\n",
    "\n",
    "*Note: It is assumed that prescribing the second drug triggers the alert.*\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "### 7. alerts\n",
    "\n",
    "**Definition:** Captures alerts generated when a patient is prescribed two drugs that adversely interact.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Attributes:**\n",
    "- `patient_id` – Foreign Key → `patients(ssn)`\n",
    "- `physician_id` – Foreign Key → `physicians(ssn)`\n",
    "- `alert_date` – Date the alert was generated\n",
    "- `drug1` – Previously prescribed drug\n",
    "- `drug2` – Newly prescribed drug causing the interaction\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "### 8. pharmacy_fills\n",
    "\n",
    "**Definition:** Tracks when and where prescriptions were filled, along with the cost.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Attributes:**\n",
    "- `prescription_id` – Foreign Key → `prescriptions(id)`\n",
    "- `pharmacy_id` – Foreign Key → `pharmacies(id)`\n",
    "- `date` – Date the prescription was filled\n",
    "- `cost` – Total cost of the prescription filled\n",
    "\n",
    "*Note: Assumes that all drugs are prescription-only.*\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "### 9. companies\n",
    "\n",
    "**Definition:** Information about pharmaceutical companies supplying drugs.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Attributes:**\n",
    "- `id` – Primary Key, unique identifier for the company\n",
    "- `name` – Company name\n",
    "- `address` – Company headquarters or office address\n",
    "- `contact_phone` – Contact number\n",
    "- **Note:** contact_name has been added separately below\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "### 10. contracts\n",
    "\n",
    "**Definition:** Represents drug supply contracts between companies and pharmacies.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Attributes:**\n",
    "- `id` – Primary Key\n",
    "- `company_id` – Foreign Key → `companies(id)`\n",
    "- `pharmacy_id` – Foreign Key → `pharmacies(id)`\n",
    "- `drug_name` – Foreign Key → `drugs(name)`\n",
    "- `dosage` – Drug dosage form\n",
    "- `quantity` – Quantity of drug in the contract\n",
    "- `date` – Date of the contract\n",
    "- `price` – Price per unit (based on quantity)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "### Schema Notes\n",
    "\n",
    "- All foreign keys ensure referential integrity across related tables.\n",
    "- Drug interactions and alerts help simulate real-world health safety protocols.\n",
    "- The schema supports tracking of prescription trends, drug pricing, supplier relationships, and patient safety alerts.\n"
